cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpsGuard in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpsGuard: Production change intelligence for Kubernetes & Terraform"
abstract: >-
  OpsGuard reviews infrastructure changes in a pull request, finds the ones that
  could take down production — public exposure, destructive changes, insecure
  config, missing reliability guardrails — explains the blast radius with a
  dependency graph, and reports back before anything is merged. Security
  decisions are made by deterministic rules; AI is used only to explain findings.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OpsGuard Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mehwish786jnc/OpsGuard"
url: "https://github.com/mehwish786jnc/OpsGuard"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - devops
  - kubernetes
  - terraform
  - security
  - ci-cd
  - infrastructure
  - policy-as-code
  - risk-analysis
